@@ -7,6 +7,14 @@ from `src/index.ts`.
 
 Run its tests with `npm test`.
 
+Use `importTasks(list, text)` from `src/index.ts` to add tasks from text, one per line as
+`title;priority;tags`, for example `Renew the insurance;high;admin money`. Each nonblank line must
+have exactly three semicolon-separated fields; leave priority empty for `normal` and tags empty for
+no tags. Fields are trimmed and tags are separated by whitespace. Blank lines are skipped. The helper
+adds valid lines in order and returns `{ imported, rejected }`, where `imported` counts added tasks
+and each rejection is `{ line, reason }` with a one-based input line number and an explanatory message.
+Invalid lines and duplicate titles are rejected without preventing later lines from being imported.
+
 Each task has a stable string `id`, unique within its list and preserved when the task is renamed or
 edited. Use `get(id)` to retrieve a task by ID. `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag`
 and `remove` accept either an ID or a title; IDs take precedence when a reference matches both.
